{
  "id": "fans___noise_power_generation",
  "title": "Fans - Noise Power Generation",
  "description": "Calculate Sound Power Level generated by fans using empirical equations. Select between SI or Imperial units and choose the appropriate formula based on available parameters (motor power, static pressure/head, or volume discharged).",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Sound Power Level Calculator\n\nSelect the unit system and formula to calculate the Sound Power Level (LN) generated by fans.\n\n**SI Units:**\n- Formula 1a: LN = 67 + 10 log(S) + 10 log(p)\n- Formula 1b: LN = 40 + 10 log(Q) + 20 log(p)\n- Formula 1c: LN = 94 + 20 log(S) - 10 log(Q)\n\n**Imperial Units:**\n- Formula 2a: LN = 90 + 10 log(s) + 10 log(h)\n- Formula 2b: LN = 55 + 10 log(q) + 20 log(h)\n- Formula 2c: LN = 125 + 20 log(s) - 10 log(q)"
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "unit_system",
          "label": "Unit System",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "SI Units (kW, Pa, m³/s)",
              "value": "si"
            },
            {
              "label": "Imperial Units (hp, in H₂O, ft³/min)",
              "value": "imperial"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "si"
        },
        {
          "id": "formula_choice",
          "label": "Formula Choice",
          "type": "select",
          "options": [
            {
              "label": "Formula 1a/2a: Motor Power + Static Pressure/Head",
              "value": "a"
            },
            {
              "label": "Formula 1b/2b: Volume Discharged + Static Pressure/Head",
              "value": "b"
            },
            {
              "label": "Formula 1c/2c: Motor Power + Volume Discharged",
              "value": "c"
            }
          ],
          "defaultValue": "a"
        },
        {
          "id": "motor_power",
          "label": "Rated Motor Power (kW or hp)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 5,
          "unit": "kW / hp"
        },
        {
          "id": "static_pressure",
          "label": "Fan Static Pressure (Pa or inch H₂O)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 500,
          "unit": "Pa / in H₂O"
        },
        {
          "id": "volume_discharged",
          "label": "Volume Discharged (m³/s or ft³/min)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 2,
          "unit": "m³/s / ft³/min"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "sound_power_level",
          "label": "Sound Power Level (LN)",
          "unit": "dB",
          "formula": "IF(inputs.unit_system='si', IF(inputs.formula_choice='a', 67 + 10*LOG10(inputs.motor_power) + 10*LOG10(inputs.static_pressure), IF(inputs.formula_choice='b', 40 + 10*LOG10(inputs.volume_discharged) + 20*LOG10(inputs.static_pressure), 94 + 20*LOG10(inputs.motor_power) - 10*LOG10(inputs.volume_discharged))), IF(inputs.formula_choice='a', 90 + 10*LOG10(inputs.motor_power) + 10*LOG10(inputs.static_pressure), IF(inputs.formula_choice='b', 55 + 10*LOG10(inputs.volume_discharged) + 20*LOG10(inputs.static_pressure), 125 + 20*LOG10(inputs.motor_power) - 10*LOG10(inputs.volume_discharged))))",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Octave (Hz)",
        "Centrifugal - Backward-Curved",
        "Centrifugal - Forward-Curved",
        "Centrifugal - Straight Radial",
        "Axial Fan"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          63,
          -4,
          -2,
          -3,
          -7
        ],
        [
          125,
          -6,
          -6,
          -5,
          -9
        ],
        [
          250,
          -9,
          -13,
          -7,
          -7
        ],
        [
          500,
          -11,
          -18,
          -7,
          -7
        ],
        [
          1000,
          -13,
          -19,
          -8,
          -8
        ],
        [
          2000,
          -16,
          -22,
          -11,
          -11
        ],
        [
          4000,
          -19,
          -25,
          -16,
          -16
        ],
        [
          8000,
          -22,
          -30,
          -18,
          -18
        ]
      ],
      "content": "### Sound Power by Frequency (dB to add to total)\nAdd these values to the calculated Sound Power Level to determine noise at specific octave frequencies based on fan type."
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Application",
        "Supply System (m/s)",
        "Exhaust System (m/s)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Sound studios, churches, libraries",
          "4 - 5",
          "5 - 7"
        ],
        [
          "Cinemas, theaters, ballrooms",
          "5 - 7",
